Enforcee — Licence
==================

This repository is **not** under a single licence. Two different things live here
and they carry different terms, deliberately.

Read this file before copying anything out of it.


1. MIT — the parts that run on your machine
-------------------------------------------

The following are licensed under the MIT Licence, reproduced in full below:

    guard/**            the hook runner that executes in your session
    cli/**              the command-line wrapper (excluding bundled engine output)
    plugin/**           the Claude Code plugin manifest, hooks, skills and commands
    .claude-plugin/**   the marketplace manifest

These are permissive on purpose. They run inside your development environment,
under your account, with access to your files. You should not have to take our
word for what they do — you should be able to read every line, fork them, audit
them, and run a modified copy. A security-adjacent tool that asks you to trust an
unreadable binary has not earned the trust it is asking for.

